# Part 1: Specific Alterations Needed From Your Stage 1 Screenshots

Looking closely at both images, here are the concrete issues and polish fixes to make before scaling up:

### 1. Expand the Bottom-Right Dock From 2+3 to 5+6 (All Future Mechanics Visible & Padlocked)
* **What's there now:** Your dock currently shows **2 Ability Slots** (`[1 🔒]`, `[2 🔒 Potion 0]`) and **3 Tabs** (`Train`, `Gear`, `Hero`).
* **What needs altering:** Under your rule that *all inaccessible features stay visible, greyed out, and padlocked*, players at Stage 1 cannot see **Action Surge**, **Heroic Inspiration**, **Class Mechanic**, **Tactics/Gambits**, **World/Bastions/Prestige**, or **Campaigns**.
* **The Fix:** Widen the bottom dock along the unused grass edge into two tidy attached trays:
  * **Ability Tray (5 circular sockets, hotkeys `1–5`):** All 5 visible & padlocked at Stage 1 → `1: Second Wind 🔒` | `2: Action Surge 🔒` | `3: Potions 🔒 (0)` | `4: Inspiration 🔒 (0)` | `5: Class Skill 🔒`.
  * **Menu Tab Tray (6 square tabs, hotkeys `T, G, H, B, W, C`):** `Train (T)` (unlocked mid-Stage 1) | `Gear (G) 🔒` | `Hero (H) 🔒` | `Gambits (B) 🔒` | `World (W) 🔒` | `Campaigns (C) 🔒`.
  * *(Note: Keep the `"Now"` goal pill—`⚔ Weapon Drills R1 [coin] 10`—floating cleanly above the Menu Tab Tray just as you already placed it!)*

### 2. Lock the Top-Right `1×` Speed & `Auto` Controls at Stage 1
* **What's there now:** In both screenshots, `▶▶1x` and `□ Auto` use the active carved-wood button style (same as the Audio button), making them look clickable at Stage 1.
* **The Fix:** Grey out and padlock both at Stage 1: **`🔒 1x`** (*tooltip: "2× Speed unlocks at Stage 20"*) and **`🔒 Auto`** (*tooltip: "Auto-Advance unlocks at Stage 10"*). Only the Audio icon stays unlocked.

### 3. Fix Three Text & Icon Clarity Issues on the Training Yard Modal (Screenshot 2)
* **Issue A — Confusing `+` beside `10 cp` on the Buy Button:** On `Weapon Drills`, `BUY · RANK 1  + 10 cp` has a little gold icon/plus right before `10 cp` that makes it look like *"gain +10 cp"* rather than *"costs 10 cp"*. Replace that `+` with the exact **copper coin sprite** from the purse (`BUY · RANK 1 · [coin] 10 cp`).
* **Issue B — Overlapping Ghost Text on the Locked `Armour Drills` Button:** Right now `"LOCKED"` sits directly on top of dim `"BUY · RANK 1"` and `"15 cp"` text, creating visual mush. Either remove `"BUY · RANK 1"` on locked buttons so it reads cleanly **`🔒 UNLOCKS STAGE 2 · [coin] 15 cp`**, or keep the ghost button clean with just **`🔒 LOCKED`** and put `Cost: 15 cp` in the card body.
* **Issue C — Conflicting Lock Reason on `Armour Drills`:** The `Armour Drills` card currently shows a padlock **AND** red text saying `"Thy purse is short."` At Stage 1, `Armour Drills` is locked by **Stage progression** (Stage 2), not just gold. Rule: **Stage-locked cards** show neutral/amber text (`"Unlocks at Stage 2"`); **unlocked-but-unaffordable cards** show red `"Thy purse is short."`

### 4. Make the Hero's Round Clock Visually Distinct From Enemy HP
* **What's there now:** In Screenshot 1, the progress bar at the Hero's feet is nearly the same red-orange colour as the Giant Rat's HP bar floating above it.
* **The Fix:** Change the Hero’s Round Clock timer under their boots (or tucked on their portrait edge) to a **gold-rimmed cyan/amber dial or bar**, keeping **red** strictly for HP so combat readability stays instant when 5+ monsters crowd the screen.

### 5. Bump Small Bitmap Body Font & Pagination Clarity
* **What's there now:** In Screenshot 2, tiny text like `"Sword work at the pell: edge and form"`, `"Each rank: a tenth harder"`, and `"T · close"` uses a very tight `5px` font where `m / n / r / t` start to blur together.
* **The Fix:** Step body text up by `+1–2px` (or use cleaner pixel kerning), add **`● ○ ○` page pips** between `<` and `>` at the bottom-left of Training Yard so players immediately know **all 6 Martial Drills** are browsable across 3 pages (`Weapon/Armour`, `Scavenging/Footwork`, `Conditioning/Tactics`), and keep a visible **greyed-out sub-tab** at the top of the modal for `Realms Mastery 🔒 (Stage 100)`.

### 6. Minor Polish Items Spotted in Screenshot 1
* **Elminster's Chimney Smoke:** Right now the wizard tower puffs pale grey smoke. Giving it occasional **green/violet/blue pixel puffs** nails the quirky Shadowdale flavour from Beat 0!
* **Top-Left `>> Action Surge [2]` Badge:** Keep this exact widget! Because Hero Level 2 now lands at **Stage 3**, having `>> Action Surge [2]` sit directly below your `XP` bar on Stage 1 acts as your permanent **"Soon" Goal preview**. (Once Lv 2 is reached, it swaps to `>> Champion [3]`, then `>> Feat / ASI [4]`, then `>> Extra Attack [5]`, etc.)
* **Elminster Dialogue vs Bottom Dock Spacing:** When Elminster's `64×64` dialogue box appears during Beats 0–10, anchor it **bottom-left** (`x=10–250`) so it never collides with the bottom-right Ability/Menu Dock or the `Weapon Drills` Goal pill.

